.TH JSONPROBE 1
.SH NAME
jsonprobe \\- run declarative readiness checks
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B jsonprobe
jsonprobe [--input SPEC.json] [--format json|ndjson]
.SH DESCRIPTION
Runs JSON-described TCP, HTTP, process, and filesystem checks. Standard input is used when --input is omitted.
.SH EVIDENCE
Aggregate JSON includes collected_at (UTC collection start time) and
collector_version. NDJSON emits individual checks without this envelope.
RCDO jsonprobe-check consumes aggregate JSON and requires named checks and fresh
collection metadata. These observations do not establish deployment safety or
cloud identity.
.SH OPTIONS
Use \fBjsonprobe --help\fR for the complete, version-specific flag list.
.SH EXIT STATUS
Uses the shared CLI status convention: 0 success, 1 a completed negative finding or policy failure, 2 invalid usage, 3 a partial result, and 4 a runtime failure. Not every status applies to every command.
